# Add a CONTROLS TUTORIAL to a simulation page

Retrofit an existing single-file simulation HTML page with a sequential
"Controls" tutorial. The reference implementation was built and verified on
`stern-gerlach-controls-tutorial.html`; this rule reproduces that exact final
behavior on other sims. **Copy the canonical blocks in §Insert below verbatim;
only adapt the parts marked ADAPT. Do not re-invent the mechanics.**

## What the finished feature does (acceptance criteria)

1. **Card zone at the top of the sidebar** ("Controls" header + small Skip
   button, slim progress dots, exactly ONE visible card at a time, footer nav:
   `‹` `›` pager on the left, primary `Next →` button on the right that reads
   `Done` on the last card).
2. **Card + control simultaneously visible, always.** This is the core
   requirement (students scrolled past hidden controls and never knew they
   were there). Achieve it by progressive reveal: every sidebar element
   covered by the tutorial — controls AND readout panels (statistics,
   legends) — starts fully hidden (`.ctl-hidden`, `display: none`). Reaching
   a card reveals its element directly beneath the card zone; earlier
   elements stay visible. Readout panels are NOT controls: hide them from the
   start and introduce them in ONE dedicated stage placed just before the
   final card. Title-bar elements (e.g. a global Reset) cannot be hidden
   without shifting the bar — dim-lock those instead (`.ctl-locked`: ~28%
   opacity, `pointer-events: none`). A `maxSeen` variable tracks the furthest
   card reached, so navigating BACK never re-hides or re-locks anything.
3. **Spotlight, no auto-scroll.** The current card's element(s) get
   `.ctl-spotlight` — an accent-colored pulsing glow, visible from the very
   first card since the element renders adjacent to the zone. Do NOT call
   `scrollIntoView`: the card must stay readable (both halves were explicit
   user corrections — auto-scroll hid the card; dim-only lock left the
   spotlight below the fold). On the readouts stage, glow the INNER data
   boxes (stat box, legend box, mode banner), never the broad section
   outlines: one box → one glow; readouts scattered across several boxes →
   glow them all together. The controller supports this via a per-step
   `spotlight` list that overrides `targets` for the glow only. The spotlight
   rule must not force a border-radius — each box keeps its own.
4. **Title-bar toggle, no sidebar restore bar.** The tutorial is VISIBLE by
   default on page load (button boots in the `.active` state). A single
   button in the title bar turns the tutorial on and off. Label swaps
   between `🧭 Hide Controls Tutorial` (visible, `.active` filled state) and
   `🧭 Controls Tutorial` (hidden, plain). There is no separate restore
   element inside the sidebar.
5. **Hide = fully usable sim; re-show = resume the tutorial state.** Hiding
   the tutorial (via the title-bar toggle, Skip, or Done on the last card)
   reveals + unlocks EVERYTHING (including readout panels) and clears every
   highlight — the sim must never be left half-disabled or half-hidden. But
   hiding must NOT advance tutorial progress (`maxSeen` stays untouched):
   re-showing resumes at the card the student left with ONLY the elements
   introduced up to that card visible, later ones re-hidden and title-bar
   lockables re-dimmed. Skip after 3 controls → reopen shows exactly those 3
   controls on card 3. Only completing the tutorial (Done) leaves everything
   introduced on reopen.
6. **Button design** matches the SR-shell "Lecture" pattern: white 36px pill,
   `1px solid rgba(19,49,49,.25)` border, slate `#334155` text, 13px/600
   sans, hover `#F5EAC4`, active state filled `#1E4D3A` with white text
   (hover `#2D6E52`).

## STEP 1 — Map the sim

- Open the target HTML file. Identify: the sidebar/right-panel container,
  every user-facing control (selects, sliders, toggle buttons), every READOUT
  panel (statistics, legends, live indicators — display-only sections), any
  global reset button, and the sim's accent color + font variables. Classify
  each sidebar element as control or readout: controls get one card each;
  readouts share one "Readouts" stage before the final card and stay hidden
  until then.
- List the controls **in the order they appear in the panel, top to bottom**.
  The tutorial follows the existing layout order. Do NOT reorder the sim's
  DOM to fit a pedagogical sequence — layout changes are a separate decision
  the user must ask for explicitly.
- Ensure each control's wrapper element has an `id` (add ids like `ctlSpin`,
  `ctlField` if missing). Standalone buttons (reset, mode toggles) can be
  targeted by their own id.
- Hide-vs-dim is decided by LOCATION, not by role: a reset button in the
  SIDEBAR is `hideable` like any control; only elements in the title bar go
  in `lockable`. If the sim has no title bar, put the tutorial toggle in
  whatever persistent header/topbar it does have.
- Topbar transport controls (Play/Pause, speed selector) ARE tutorial content
  when the sim animates: they go in `lockable` and get cards like any
  control, ordered where the student first needs them — usually a Play card
  first, since nothing moves without it. A sim that renders statically (no
  play loop) has no transport cards.
- Hide the control boxes and readout sections, but keep the sidebar's own
  section heading for the controls area (e.g. "Apparatus Controls") visible
  from boot — it frames where the revealed controls appear.
- Static/help panels (keyboard-shortcut lists, usage hints) are neither
  controls nor readouts: add their id to `hideable` with NO step targets —
  hidden for the whole tutorial, auto-revealed on hide/skip/done, never given
  a card (same mechanism as guided-inquiry zones).
- Sections whose visibility the SIM ITSELF manages (mode tabs switching panel
  sections): never add those sections or their contents to `hideable` — the
  tutorial must not fight the sim's show/hide logic. Introduce the mode
  switch as a control card, cover the elements of the BOOT mode, and let the
  readouts card's copy mention what the other mode shows in the same space.
- If the sidebar already carries a "Controls" heading of its own, title the
  zone "Controls Tutorial" instead of "Controls" to avoid stacked duplicate
  headings.
- A bare button sitting in a wrapper div: put the id on the WRAPPER for
  hide/reveal (hiding only the button strands an empty spacing div) but
  spotlight the BUTTON itself via the step's `spotlight` list.
- Readout boxes that stand alone (not inside a section with other content)
  can be step `targets` directly — reveal target and glow target coincide,
  no separate `spotlight` list needed.
- Check for name collisions before inserting: if the target sim already uses
  any `.ctl-*` class or `ctlZone`/`ctlDots`/`ctlCards`/`ctlPrev`/`ctlPgNext`/
  `ctlNext`/`ctlSkip`/`ctlTutorialToggle` id, rename this rule's versions
  with a prefix consistently across CSS, markup, and JS.

## STEP 2 — Insert the three canonical blocks

### 2a. CSS — tutorial zone, lock, spotlight (before `</style>`)

ADAPT: every `#3b9b8f` / `rgba(59,155,143,…)` is the sim accent — swap for
the target sim's accent so dots, glow, and "Try:" tags match its theme. The
collapse rule `.ctl-collapsed .ctl-zone` is deliberately panel-agnostic — do
NOT scope it to the sim's panel class. `var(--font-sans)` must exist in the
target (or replace with its sans font stack). Dark-panel text colors
(`#e5e7eb`, `#b6c2cf`) suit a dark sidebar; lighten for light sims. If the
sim has a LIGHT/DARK THEME TOGGLE, hard-coded colors are wrong in one theme:
map the block's literals to the sim's CSS variables instead — accent literals
→ its `--accent` (and `--accent-bg` for button fills), heading and body text
→ its `--text-primary`/`--text-secondary`, zone border → its `--border`.
Keep the title-bar button palette (§2b) as-is — it is the cross-sim house
style, not per-sim theming.

    /* ===== Controls tutorial (card structure, mirrors guided-inquiry shell) ===== */
    .ctl-zone { padding: 16px 18px; border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(19, 49, 49, 0.4); }
    .ctl-zone-head { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 8px; margin-bottom: 10px; }
    .ctl-zone-head h3 {
        margin: 0; flex: 1; font-size: 12px; font-weight: 700; color: #e5e7eb;
        text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 1.2px; font-family: var(--font-sans);
    }
    .ctl-skip {
        width: auto !important; margin: 0 !important; padding: 4px 10px !important;
        font-size: 11px !important; letter-spacing: 0.04em; color: #94a3b8 !important;
        background: transparent !important; border: 1px solid rgba(148,163,184,0.3) !important;
        border-radius: 6px !important; cursor: pointer;
    }
    .ctl-skip:hover { color: #e2e8f0 !important; border-color: rgba(148,163,184,0.55) !important; }
    .ctl-dots { display: flex; gap: 6px; margin-bottom: 12px; }
    .ctl-dot { flex: 1; height: 4px; border-radius: 2px; background: rgba(148,163,184,0.22); transition: background .2s; }
    .ctl-dot.done   { background: rgba(59,155,143,0.45); }
    .ctl-dot.active { background: #3b9b8f; }
    .ctl-step { display: none; }
    .ctl-step.active { display: block; animation: ctlFade .25s ease; }
    @keyframes ctlFade { from { opacity: 0; transform: translateY(4px); } to { opacity: 1; transform: none; } }
    .ctl-step h4 { margin: 0 0 8px; font-size: 13px; font-weight: 700; color: #e2e8f0; font-family: var(--font-sans); }
    .ctl-step h4 .ctl-step-tag { color: #3b9b8f; }
    .ctl-try { margin-top: 7px !important; }
    .ctl-try .ctl-try-tag { color: #3b9b8f; font-weight: 700; }
    .ctl-step p { margin: 0; font-size: 12.5px; line-height: 1.55; color: #b6c2cf; font-family: var(--font-sans); }
    .ctl-step p b, .ctl-step p strong { color: #e2e8f0; }
    .ctl-nav { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: center; margin-top: 12px; }
    .ctl-pager { display: flex; gap: 8px; }
    .ctl-nav button {
        width: auto !important; margin: 0 !important; padding: 6px 12px !important;
        font-size: 12.5px !important; font-weight: 600; border-radius: 6px !important;
        background: rgba(30, 77, 58, 0.18) !important; border: 1px solid rgba(59,155,143,0.45) !important;
        color: #cfe9e4 !important; cursor: pointer; line-height: 1;
    }
    .ctl-nav button:hover:not(:disabled) { background: rgba(59,155,143,0.28) !important; }
    .ctl-nav button:disabled { opacity: .35; cursor: default; }
    .ctl-nav .ctl-pager-btn { min-width: 34px; text-align: center; }
    #ctlNext { min-width: 88px; text-align: center; }
    .ctl-collapsed .ctl-zone { display: none; }

    /* Progressive control exposure: sidebar elements are HIDDEN until their
       card introduces them, so the current control always sits directly under
       the tutorial card (card + spotlight simultaneously visible, no scroll). */
    .ctl-hidden { display: none !important; }
    .ctl-locked { opacity: 0.28; pointer-events: none; filter: saturate(0.4); transition: opacity .25s, filter .25s; }
    .ctl-spotlight {
        border-color: #3b9b8f !important; border-radius: 6px;
        box-shadow: 0 0 0 1px #3b9b8f, 0 0 14px rgba(59,155,143,0.55);
        animation: ctlPulse 1.6s ease-in-out infinite;
    }
    @keyframes ctlPulse {
        0%, 100% { box-shadow: 0 0 0 1px #3b9b8f, 0 0 10px rgba(59,155,143,0.4); }
        50%      { box-shadow: 0 0 0 2px #3b9b8f, 0 0 20px rgba(59,155,143,0.75); }
    }

### 2b. CSS — title-bar buttons (house style, do NOT retheme per sim)

    /* SR-shell style header buttons (white pill, 36px, filled dark-green when active) */
