### 2c. Markup — card zone (FIRST child of the sidebar container)

ADAPT: card count, numbering, titles, copy (per STEP 3 template). Keep ids
`ctlZone/ctlDots/ctlCards/ctlPrev/ctlPgNext/ctlNext/ctlSkip` exactly — the
controller binds to them. Example cards shown are from the Stern–Gerlach
reference; write this sim's own.

    <div class="ctl-zone" id="ctlZone">
        <div class="ctl-zone-head">
            <h3>Controls</h3>
            <button type="button" class="ctl-skip" id="ctlSkip" title="Unlock every control and hide the tutorial">Skip</button>
        </div>
        <div class="ctl-dots" id="ctlDots"></div>
        <div class="ctl-zone-body" id="ctlCards">

            <div class="ctl-step">
                <h4><span class="ctl-step-tag">1 ·</span> Total Spin (j)</h4>
                <p>Sets the spin <b>j</b> of the atoms in the beam. The screen shows <b>2j&nbsp;+&nbsp;1</b> bands — one per allowed m<sub>j</sub> value.</p>
                <p class="ctl-try"><span class="ctl-try-tag">Try:</span> pick <b>j = 1</b> and count three bands.</p>
            </div>

            <!-- …one card per control, then ONE Readouts card… -->

            <div class="ctl-step">
                <h4><span class="ctl-step-tag">✓</span> All controls unlocked</h4>
                <p>Explore freely. Reopen this tutorial any time from the <b>title-bar</b> button.</p>
            </div>

        </div>
        <div class="ctl-nav">
            <div class="ctl-pager">
                <button type="button" id="ctlPrev" class="ctl-pager-btn" aria-label="Previous" disabled>&lt;</button>
                <button type="button" id="ctlPgNext" class="ctl-pager-btn" aria-label="Next">&gt;</button>
            </div>
            <button type="button" id="ctlNext">Next →</button>
        </div>
    </div>

**If the sidebar already has a guided-inquiry / lesson card zone** (many
shell sims do): place `ctl-zone` ABOVE it, give the inquiry zone an id, and
add that id to `hideable` WITHOUT putting it in any step's `targets`. Effect:
the inquiry stays hidden while the controls tutorial is visible (learn the
controls first) and appears automatically whenever the tutorial is hidden,
skipped, or completed. Never hide the sim's meta-UI header buttons (Lecture,
Info ⓘ, Formal ∑, theme toggles) and never add them to `lockable` — they are
not tutorial content; leave them fully functional.

### 2d. Markup — title-bar toggle

Place beside existing header controls, in the LEFT/title-side cluster
directly beside the info (i) icon or existing header toggles — NOT in the
right-side action cluster with Reset. Starts `.active` because the tutorial
is visible on load:

    <button type="button" class="title-bar-btn active" id="ctlTutorialToggle" title="Show or hide the controls tutorial">🧭 Hide Controls Tutorial</button>

### 2e. JS — controller (before `</body>`)

Insert exactly as shown — INCLUDING the `<script>` wrapper (without it the
controller is inert page text and nothing runs). ADAPT only:

- `steps`: one entry per card, `targets` = element id(s) that card
  reveals/unlocks; second-to-last entry is the readouts stage (all
  readout-SECTION ids as `targets`, plus a `spotlight` list of the inner
  data-box ids), final done-card entry is `{ targets: [] }`. If the sim has
  no readout panels, drop the readouts entry entirely (and its card) — the
  arrays and dots derive from `steps`/cards automatically.
- `spotlight` (optional per step): the ids that get the glow, when they
  differ from `targets`. For readouts, reveal whole sections via `targets`
  but glow ONLY the inner boxes that visually contain the data — never the
  broad section outline. Give those inner boxes ids if they lack them.
- `hideable`: every SIDEBAR id (controls + readout sections + any inquiry
  zone / help panel with no step targets).
- `lockable`: TITLE-BAR ids only.
- `panel` selector if the sidebar container isn't `.right-panel`.

Semantics that must survive adaptation: `maxSeen` governs reveal/unlock
(back-nav never re-hides or re-locks); NO scrollIntoView; `setVisible(false)`
reveals + unlocks everything and clears highlights but MUST NOT modify
`maxSeen` — hiding is temporary full exposure, not completion; `setVisible(true)`
just calls `apply()`; Done, Skip, and the title-bar toggle all route through
`setVisible`.

    <script>
    /* ===== Controls tutorial controller ===== */
    (function () {
        // targets = elements revealed/unlocked by the card.
        // spotlight (optional) = elements that get the glow; defaults to targets.
        const steps = [
            { targets: ['ctlSpin'] },
            { targets: ['ctlField'] },
            { targets: ['ctlRate'] },
            { targets: ['classicalToggle'] },
            { targets: ['headerReset'] },
            { targets: ['ctlStats', 'ctlLegend'],
              spotlight: ['modeIndicator', 'ctlStatsBox', 'ctlLegendBox'] }, // readouts stage
            { targets: [] } // done card
        ];
        const spotlightable = Array.from(new Set(
            steps.flatMap(st => st.spotlight || st.targets)));
        // Sidebar elements: fully hidden until their card introduces them.
        const hideable = ['ctlSpin', 'ctlField', 'ctlRate', 'classicalToggle', 'ctlStats', 'ctlLegend'];
        // Title-bar elements can't be hidden without shifting the bar: dim-lock instead.
        const lockable = ['headerReset'];
        const zone = document.getElementById('ctlZone');
        const panel = document.querySelector('.right-panel');
        const cards = Array.from(document.querySelectorAll('#ctlCards .ctl-step'));
        const dotsHost = document.getElementById('ctlDots');
        const prevBtn = document.getElementById('ctlPrev');
        const pgNext = document.getElementById('ctlPgNext');
        const nextBtn = document.getElementById('ctlNext');
        const skipBtn = document.getElementById('ctlSkip');
        const tutToggle = document.getElementById('ctlTutorialToggle');
        let step = 0, maxSeen = 0;

        cards.forEach(() => {
            const d = document.createElement('div');
            d.className = 'ctl-dot';
            dotsHost.appendChild(d);
        });
        const dots = Array.from(dotsHost.children);

        function el(id) { return document.getElementById(id); }

        function apply() {
            cards.forEach((c, i) => c.classList.toggle('active', i === step));
            dots.forEach((d, i) => {
                d.classList.toggle('active', i === step);
                d.classList.toggle('done', i < step);
            });
            prevBtn.disabled = step <= 0;
            pgNext.disabled = step >= cards.length - 1;
            nextBtn.textContent = step >= cards.length - 1 ? 'Done' : 'Next →';

            // Everything introduced up to the furthest step reached stays visible
            const introduced = new Set();
            for (let i = 0; i <= maxSeen; i++) steps[i].targets.forEach(t => introduced.add(t));
            hideable.forEach(id => el(id).classList.toggle('ctl-hidden', !introduced.has(id)));
            lockable.forEach(id => el(id).classList.toggle('ctl-locked', !introduced.has(id)));

            // Spotlight only the current card's element(s)
            spotlightable.forEach(id => el(id).classList.remove('ctl-spotlight'));
            // No auto-scroll: let the student read the card first, then scroll themselves.
            (steps[step].spotlight || steps[step].targets)
                .forEach(id => el(id).classList.add('ctl-spotlight'));
        }

        function show(n) {
            step = Math.max(0, Math.min(n, cards.length - 1));
            maxSeen = Math.max(maxSeen, step);
            apply();
        }

        function setVisible(on) {
            panel.classList.toggle('ctl-collapsed', !on);
            tutToggle.textContent = on ? '\u{1F9ED} Hide Controls Tutorial' : '\u{1F9ED} Controls Tutorial';
            tutToggle.classList.toggle('active', on);
            if (!on) {
                // Hiding the tutorial reveals + unlocks everything and clears
                // highlights — but does NOT touch maxSeen, so tutorial progress
                // is preserved while hidden.
                hideable.forEach(id => el(id).classList.remove('ctl-hidden'));
                lockable.forEach(id => el(id).classList.remove('ctl-locked'));
                spotlightable.forEach(id => el(id).classList.remove('ctl-spotlight'));
            } else {
                apply();   // restore reveal state from maxSeen + current spotlight
            }
        }

        prevBtn.addEventListener('click', () => show(step - 1));
        pgNext.addEventListener('click', () => show(step + 1));
        nextBtn.addEventListener('click', () => {
            if (step >= cards.length - 1) setVisible(false);
            else show(step + 1);
        });
        skipBtn.addEventListener('click', () => setVisible(false));
        tutToggle.addEventListener('click', () =>
            setVisible(panel.classList.contains('ctl-collapsed')));

        show(0);
    })();
    </script>

## STEP 3 — Write the cards

One card per control, in panel order — except tightly-coupled pairs (a toggle
plus its own rate/amount slider, e.g. Auto Measure + its per-second rate)
which share ONE card with both elements revealed and spotlighted together.
Then ONE "Readouts" card that reveals all readout panels together; then a
final `✓ All controls unlocked` card. If the sim has NO readout panels, skip
the Readouts stage entirely — controls then done card. Number cards
`1 ·, 2 ·, …` continuing through the Readouts card; the final card's tag is
`✓`. Every card follows this exact template:

    <h4><span class="ctl-step-tag">N ·</span> Control Name</h4>
    <p>[WHAT IT SETS — one sentence, plain language first, symbols like
       ∂B/∂z only as a parenthetical] [OBSERVABLE EFFECT — what visibly
       changes on screen, with the key quantity in <b>bold</b>]</p>
    <p class="ctl-try"><span class="ctl-try-tag">Try:</span> [ONE concrete
       action with a specific value, e.g. "pick <b>j = 1</b> and count
       three bands."]</p>

Copy rules (all user-validated):

- **25–45 words per card, total.** If a card exceeds this, cut adjectives and
  physics-speak, not the Try line.
- **Try actions must not imply magic numbers.** For sliders, ask for a
  qualitative extreme ("drag it to its maximum") — never a bare value like
  "set it to 6 T/m", which reads as if that number were special. A specific
  value is allowed ONLY when the number itself is the lesson (e.g. "pick
  j = 1 and count three bands", where 2j + 1 = 3 is the point).
- Describe the effect as **what the student sees on screen**, not
  beam/internal-state language ("the screen shows 2j + 1 bands", not "the
  beam splits into 2j + 1 channels").
- If a control changes appearance when used (e.g. a button that relabels
  itself), say so in one clause — self-relabeling buttons confuse students.
- If a control changes no physics (e.g. emission rate), state that explicitly
  ("changes **no physics** — only how fast the pattern builds").
- A reset card explains *why*: "so the new pattern isn't mixed with the old
  one." No location hints — the spotlight is the location cue.
- Final card: everything is unlocked, explore freely, and reopen "any time
  from the **title-bar** button". Never reference UI that no longer exists.
- If a control's visible effect depends on a LATER control's setting (e.g. an
  animation-speed slider whose motion only shows in a view mode introduced
  next), the card must still be true at its own moment — find what IS
  observable right then (often the more interesting physics point, e.g.
  "|ψ|² never moves — probability doesn't depend on phase").
- **Every factual claim in a card must be verified against THIS sim's actual
  code/behavior** before shipping — slider ranges, what a readout counts,
  what stays constant. Never inherit a claim from another sim's cards; in
  bulk runs this is the main source of silently wrong copy.

## STEP 4 — Verify before delivering

If the bundled verifier is available (repo path
`controls-tutorial-skill-v2/scripts/verify.js`; requires `npm i jsdom` once),
run it — exit code 0 = ship, 1 = fix before delivering:

    node controls-tutorial-skill-v2/scripts/verify.js <patched.html> --baseline <original.html>

`--baseline` matters: sims that load KaTeX/Three.js from CDNs throw in jsdom
regardless of the tutorial — those pre-existing errors are subtracted so only
errors the tutorial introduced fail the build.

If the script is not available, verify the same invariants by hand in a
headless jsdom walkthrough (boot with `runScripts:'dangerously'`, stub
`getContext`, instrument `scrollIntoView`), asserting in order:

1. **Boot:** card 0 active, ONLY the first control visible in the sidebar
   (every other control and all readout sections carry `.ctl-hidden`), first
   control spotlighted, title-bar lockables dimmed, toggle `.active` with a
   "Hide" label, dots count == card count, no scroll fired.
2. **Forward walk:** reveal is monotone (hidden set only shrinks); every
   non-final card has ≥1 spotlight; a spotlighted element is never hidden;
   final card has NO spotlight and the Next button reads `Done`.
3. **Back-nav** from a mid card: hidden/locked sets stay at the
   furthest-step state (nothing re-hides or re-locks); spotlight matches the
   forward pass for that card.
4. **Mid-tutorial hide → re-show** (test this in a FRESH pass BEFORE the
   last card is ever reached — testing after a full walk cannot catch the
   maxSeen regression): hide → everything revealed + unlocked, no spotlight,
   `#ctlZone` computed display is `none`, toggle inactive with swapped
   label; re-show → same card, hidden/locked/spotlight sets exactly
   restored. Repeat the same check via **Skip**.
5. **Done:** collapses the zone; reopen lands on the final card with only
   untargeted hideables (inquiry zone, help panels) hidden.
6. **Zero `scrollIntoView` calls ever**, and no NEW runtime errors relative
   to the original file.

Two things no script can judge — check manually per sim: the readouts stage
glows inner data boxes rather than section outlines, and the card copy's
factual claims hold for this sim.

Deliver the modified HTML as a new file (`<simname>-controls-tutorial.html`)
— never overwrite the original in place.

## Bulk application (a batch of sims)

- Process one sim at a time and re-run the FULL workflow for each: map,
  classify, insert, write copy, verify. Never reuse another sim's `steps`
  arrays, ids, accent color, or card text — structural similarity between
  sims is not id similarity.
- Always boot the ORIGINAL file first to collect its pre-existing jsdom
  errors, and pass it via `--baseline` when verifying the patched file.
- A sim that fails any invariant does not ship with the batch — fix it or
  set it aside; never lower the bar to keep a batch moving.
- Keep a per-sim note of anything that forced a deviation from this rule (a
  layout that resisted the FIRST-child rule, a control that fit neither
  hideable nor lockable). Deviations are skill feedback: report them to the
  user at the end of the batch rather than silently improvising differently
  in each file.

## Common pitfalls (each one happened during the reference build)

- Dim-only locking with readout panels left visible — the readouts push the
  controls below the fold and students never see the spotlight. Hide
  un-introduced sidebar elements entirely; dim-lock is for the title bar only.
- Overlay/popover tutorials look tempting for co-visibility but are fragile
  across sim layouts and block interaction with the control being taught —
  rejected during the reference build; keep the in-sidebar reveal.
- Adding `scrollIntoView` on spotlight — it hides the card. Don't.
- Leaving a sidebar "restore" element after moving the toggle to the title
  bar — one affordance only.
- Card text referencing removed UI ("the bar below") — re-read every card
  after structural changes.
- Restyling an existing header toggle (e.g. a hover-hints switch): keep its
  hidden checkbox and event wiring untouched; wrap it in a `title-bar-btn`
  label and drive the active look with CSS `:has()`. Preserve inverted logic
  if the sim has it (unchecked = feature ON).
- Forgetting that `Done`, `Skip`, and the title-bar toggle must all route
  through the same `setVisible(false)` path so unlock behavior is identical.
- The collapse rule must stay panel-agnostic: `.ctl-collapsed .ctl-zone
  { display: none; }` with NO panel class prefix. An early version hardcoded
  `.right-panel...` — on any sim with a different panel class the zone
  silently never hides, and toggling appears to hide the controls/readouts
  instead of the cards. Verify the zone's computed display; keep the rule
  prefix-free.
- Pasting the controller without its `<script>` wrapper — it becomes inert
  page text, nothing runs, and verification fails with "dots (0)". Keep the
  wrapper.
- Setting `maxSeen = last` inside `setVisible(false)` to force full
  exposure — that marks everything as introduced, so reopening after a
  mid-way Skip wrongly shows the whole sidebar instead of the saved tutorial
  state. Full exposure while hidden comes from removing the classes, never
  from advancing `maxSeen`.

## Self-check

- [ ] Card zone is the FIRST child of the sidebar; one card per control in
      panel order (coupled pairs share one card); one Readouts stage before
      the final `✓` card (omitted only if the sim has no readouts).
- [ ] Every covered sidebar element boots `.ctl-hidden`; title-bar lockables
      boot `.ctl-locked`; current card's elements glow `.ctl-spotlight`; no
      `scrollIntoView` anywhere.
- [ ] `maxSeen` semantics intact: back-nav never re-hides; hide/Skip/Done all
      route through `setVisible(false)`; hiding never touches `maxSeen`;
      re-show resumes the exact saved state.
- [ ] Title-bar toggle boots `.active` / "🧭 Hide Controls Tutorial"; no
      sidebar restore element; house-style button palette untouched.
- [ ] Any existing guided-inquiry zone is in `hideable` with no step targets;
      meta-UI header buttons (Lecture, ⓘ, ∑, theme) untouched.
- [ ] Card copy: 25–45 words, no magic numbers in Try lines, on-screen
      language, every claim verified against THIS sim's code.
- [ ] Verifier passes (or the manual invariant walkthrough in STEP 4 does);
      delivered as a new `<simname>-controls-tutorial.html` file.
